diff --git a/par/ims/README.md b/par/ims/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a012c68f65eb2c46cf7b562972fd68d3acf65110
--- /dev/null
+++ b/par/ims/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# PAR Open IMS compatibility service
+
+This platform-signed system application bridges Android's `ImsService` API to
+the legacy Huawei `vendor.huawei.hardware.radio.ims@1.0` service exposed by the
+Kirin 970 vendor image. It contains no Huawei APK, extracted Java archive,
+native library, resource, signing key, modem implementation, or firmware.
+
+The MMTEL and call-session implementation is derived from the GPL-3.0-or-later
+[`penn5/hwims-java`](https://github.com/penn5/hwims-java) project and its
+[`Iceows/hwims-java`](https://github.com/Iceows/hwims-java) continuation. PAR
+changes remove the proprietary video library and Mapcon dependencies, target
+the dedicated IMS HAL, and implement the nova 3 single-IMS DSDS policy. IMS
+enable/disable uses the public Huawei Radio and HisiRadio HIDL Binder ABI to
+toggle the modem IMS switch and request registration; it does not bundle or
+load Huawei framework code.
+
+The adjacent HIDL files are compatibility interface metadata used by AOSP
+`hidl-gen`. They generate the client-side Binder boilerplate at build time and
+do not contain Huawei's service implementation.
